 "manufacturer": "UNI-ROYAL (Uniroyal Elec)",
 "title": "HP and SP series thick film chip resistors for high power, 0402 to 2512",
 "source": {
  "document": "Royalohm HP, SP series",
  "pages": 2
 },
 "summary": "Thick film chip resistors that carry more power than the usual rating for their case size, in nine types from HP02 (0402, 1/10W) to HP12 (2512, 2W) and SP12 (2512, 3W, thicker body). Values reach 10 MΩ, with a low end of 10 mΩ, 0.1 Ω or 1 Ω depending on type, in ±1% and ±5%, and every HP type is also a zero-ohm jumper. The body is a high purity alumina substrate with a protective coat over the resistive element, and the ends are Ni/Cr, a nickel barrier and lead-free tin. They take wave or reflow soldering; uses named are AV adapters, LCD backlights and camera strobes.",
